<title>GERMANY: PWA Q1 pretax profit down, oper profit up.</title>
<headline>PWA Q1 pretax profit down, oper profit up.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			     70	vs 85</p>
<p>    Operating profit			   90	vs 52</p>
<p>    Sales				  about 1,200   n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German paper manufacturer is PWA Papierwerke Waldhof Aschaffenburg AG. The company said the pre-tax profit includes 15 million marks in costs for a restructuring of its hygiene products business. The year-earlier profit included one-time income of 46 million marks from the sale of plastics subsidiary PWA Kunststoff. The operating profit figure of 90 million marks excludes those special effects, the company said. It added that compared with the final quarter of 1996, operating profit rose 48 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
